<h3 data-cp="head">Step 1 · Tell the story of your learning in Sprint 3</h3>
<p class="body" id="q-story">Describe your learning journey in Sprint 3 as a story. Choose three or four of these questions to build it around; you do not have to answer all of them. What motivated you to learn this particular topic? How did you go about it? Did you use AI, and how? When did you work on it, and for how much time? What surprised you? Who or what helped?</p>
<div class="task"><div class="rbox"><label class="qt" for="bx-story"><b>My Sprint 3 story.</b></label><textarea class="box large" id="bx-story" data-key="story" data-cp="box" aria-describedby="q-story" placeholder="I chose how a bike stays upright because I ride every day and had never thought about it. I started on the Tuesday after the goal form was due, mostly late evenings, maybe six hours in all. I asked my Dojo for a place to start and it pointed me at angular momentum; the OpenStax chapter got me the formula. What surprised me was that the relationship was simple but choosing realistic numbers for the scenarios took longer than the physics. My guide group helped by asking why a stationary bike falls over, which became my first look-alike scenario."></textarea><div class="airow"><button type="button" class="btn" data-ai="story">AI feedback</button></div><div class="aibox" data-aibox="story" role="status" aria-live="polite"></div>
<details class="moreex"><summary>Two more examples</summary>
<blockquote>My topic was why a phone&#x27;s screen rotates. I worked on it in two sittings, both the night before each due date, about three hours each. I used the learning trail for the first part and PhET to check the formula. The surprise was how long Scenario 4 took: I kept picking situations that were just different, not similar-looking. My Dojo helped by asking what single detail I could change in Scenario 1.</blockquote>
<blockquote>I wanted to understand why a thrown ball lands where it does, because I pitch. I spent most of my time on the goal form, about four hours, going back and forth on what exactly I was predicting; the scenarios then took one evening. I did not use AI for the physics, only to check my units. Nobody helped, and looking back I think asking someone earlier would have saved me the time on the goal form.</blockquote>
</details></div></div>

